# Archives for the GCC chain (gcc-direct/*.sh), as `NAME SHA256 DERIVATION`.
# The chain's tools read gzip, bzip2 and plain tar, not xz, so binutils is
# pinned as the plain tar inside the release tarball that gcc64/SOURCES pins:
#   xz -dc binutils-2.30.tar.xz > build-out/stage-b-inputs/binutils-2.30.tar
# (any xz gives the same bytes; the .xz is checked against gcc64/SOURCES first).
# The other two are gcc64/SOURCES pins unchanged.
